  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In many ways, Strixhaven Initiate feels like an updated version of "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Magic Initiate",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/magic-initiate/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The cantrip options are iconic options from several classes which were published in the Player’s Handbook alongside Magic Initiate, so limiting characters to those options prevents players from taking potentially problematic cantrips like Booming Blade which are added in other supplements. In exchange for that loss of flexibility, we gain the ability to pick our spellcasting ability score, somewhat more flexibility in your choice of class for the granted 1st-level spell, and the ability to re-cast the leveled spell using spell slots regardless of your class (Magic Initiate only allows you to re-cast the spell if you have levels in the class you picked for the feat)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Rather than picking a single class, Strixhaven Initiate instead allows you to pick from one of the 5 "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Strixhaven colleges",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/sacoc/character-options#ChoosingaCollege"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Your choice of college determines your spell options, so choosing your college is just as important as choosing a class for Magic Initiate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Due to the ability to re-cast the leveled spell you select, the biggest beneficiaries of Strixhaven Initiate are full spellcasters. Partial casters like artificers or eldritch knight fighters can also benefit, but their reduced number of spell slots reduces the usefulness of the feat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For more information about spellcasting feats, including ratings of the various feats, see our "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Spellcasting Feats Guide",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/spellcasting-feats/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
