    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "heading": "Strixhaven Initiate College Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-lorehold",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "heading": "Lorehold",
      "sourceAnchor": "lorehold",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-lorehold-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Nothing amazing here. If you want cleric spells, Silverquill is a better\n\tchoice. If you’re going Lorehold, you want Sacred Flame and a leveled wizard spell.\n\tGood options include Bless, Heroism, and Shield of Faith from the Cleric and\n\tAbsorb Elements, Mage Armor, Shield, and Silvery Barbs from the Wizard. This\n\tcould be a good option for bards or druids."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cantrips",
      "parentSectionId": "section-lorehold",
      "heading": "Lorehold Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cantrips-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Light"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A staple utility, but available to most full spellcasters."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sacred Flame"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Simple and effective ranged damage."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thaumaturgy"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational and too limited. See our \n\t\t"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Practical Guide to Prestidigitation",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/prestidigitation/#thaumaturgy"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n\t\tfor more advice."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-prismari",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "heading": "Prismari",
      "sourceAnchor": "prismari",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-prismari-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Nothing amazing here. The cantrips are staple wizard options, and access to\n\teither bard or sorcerer spells is tempting. Bard offers options like Healing\n\tWord and Faerie Fire, while Sorcerer offers options like Absorb Elements,\n\tChromatic Orb, Mage Armor, Magic Missile, Shield, and Silvery Barbs. This is\n\tan effective choice for clerics and druids."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cantrips-2",
      "parentSectionId": "section-prismari",
      "heading": "Prismary Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cantrips-2-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fire Bolt"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Simple, reliable damage at range. The only problem is that fire\n\t\tresistance is common. But since the Bard is the only one who might\n\t\treasonably take this and Eldritch Blast is an option, this appeals to\n\t\tliterally no one."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Prestidigitation"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Really cool, but not impactful enough to your build that it’s worth a\n\t\tfeat on its own. See our \n\t\t"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Practical Guide to Prestidigitation",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/prestidigitation/#prestidigitation"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n\t\tfor more advice."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ray of Frost"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Decent single-target ranged damage, but if all you want is damage you\n\t\tshould grab a bow. The speed penalty is nice, but it won’t win you any\n\t\tfights on its own."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-quandrix",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "heading": "Quandrix",
      "sourceAnchor": "quandrix",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-quandrix-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "All three cantrip options are utility options. Guidance is a staple and\n\teveryone who can get it should, but that’s not enough to make Quandrix a great\n\toption. Good leveled spell options include Goodberry and Healing Word from the\n\tDruid and Absorb Elements, Mage Armor, and Shield from the Wizard. This is a\n\tgood option for clerics who want wizard spells and for sorcerers, warlocks,\n\tand wizards who want Guidance and Healing Word."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cantrips-3",
      "parentSectionId": "section-quandrix",
      "heading": "Quandrix Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cantrips-3-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Guidance"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic and versatile. You should probably cast this at every\n\t\topportunity outside of combat."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mage Hand"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good utility options."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-silverquill",
      "parentSectionId": "section-quandrix",
      "heading": "Silverquill",
      "sourceAnchor": "silverquill",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-silverquill-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two good offensive cantrips from different classes. Good leveled spell\n\toptions include Faerie Fire from the Bard, Bless and Heroism from the Cleric,\n\tand Healing Word from either. This is a great option for many spellcasters,\n\tincluding druids, sorcerers, warlocks, and wizards, but bards and clerics may\n\tboth still find Silverquill appealing."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cantrips-4",
      "parentSectionId": "section-quandrix",
      "heading": "Silverquill Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cantrips-4-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sacred Flame"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Simple and effective ranged damage."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thaumaturgy"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational and too limited. See our \n\t\t"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Practical Guide to Prestidigitation",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/prestidigitation/#thaumaturgy"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n\t\tfor more advice."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Vicious Mockery"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Easily the most iconic bard spell, Vicious Mockery is unique, flavorful,\n\t\tand mechanically fantastic. The damage is relatively small, but the debuff\n\t\tis absolutely worth the poor damage."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-witherbloom",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strixhaven-initiate-college-options",
      "heading": "Witherbloom",
      "sourceAnchor": "witherbloom",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-witherbloom-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Just go for Quandrix. You get the same leveled spell options with better\n\tcantrips."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cantrips-5",
      "parentSectionId": "section-witherbloom",
      "heading": "Witherbloom Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "cantrips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cantrips-5-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
